        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> If I copy your configuration, and open markdown file, Neovim prompts me with `E5108: Error executing lua: vim/_editor.lua:0: nvim_exec2(): Vim:E492: Not an editor command: MarkdownPreview.`\r\n> \r\n> Does this mean that all plugins using `BufEnter` autocmds need to be included in `MiniDeps.now`?\r\n\r\nUse `now()` if you want/need functionality to be available immediately after opening Neovim. Use `later()` otherwise.\r\n\r\nThis includes situations like `nvim -- README.md` and `:MarkdownPreview` command. If 'iamcco/markdown-preview.nvim' is loaded in `later()` then `nvim -- README.md` won't have `:MarkdownPreview` command because [it is created per buffer](https://github.com/iamcco/markdown-preview.nvim/blob/a923f5fc5ba36a3b17e289dc35dc17f66d0548ee/plugin/mkdp.vim#L138-L142) and those events were already triggered for 'README.md' file *before* `later()` callback was executed.\r\n\r\nSo if you want to be able to do `nvim -- README.md`, use `now()` (always or conditionally on whether there are arguments in this sesssion). Otherwise use `later()`.",
            "created_at": "2024-12-04T09:26:49Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1378#issuecomment-2516673080",
            "id": 2516673080,
